hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21012","Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us, he said: Azrah al-Ansari narrated to me, Ilba ibn Ahmar narrated to us, Abu Zayd narrated to us, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: come close to me, so I came close to him, and he said: put your hand in and wipe my back. He said: so I put my hand inside his shirt and wiped his back, and the seal of prophethood fell between my fingers. He said: then he was asked about the seal of prophethood, and he said: hairs between his shoulders."
"21013","Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us, Azrah ibn Thabit al-Ansari narrated to us, Ilba ibn Ahmar narrated to us, Abu Zayd al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: come near me, he said, then he wiped with his hand over his head and his beard, he said, then he said: O Allah, beautify him and preserve his beauty. He said: he lived to a little over one hundred years, and there was no whiteness in his head or his beard except a slight trace, and he was open-faced, and his face did not wrinkle until he died."
"21014","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Amr ibn Bujdan, from Abu Zayd al-Ansari, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed among our dwellings and found the smell of cooking meat, and he said: who is this who slaughtered? He said: then a man from among us came out to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, this was a day in which food was disliked, so I slaughtered to eat and to feed my neighbors. He said: then repeat it. He said: no, by the One besides whom there is no god, I have nothing except a young sheep of sheep or a lamb, he said it three times. He said: then slaughter it, and it will not suffice for anyone after you."
